    "chunks": [
      { "str": "1", "x": 108, "y": 710.04, "width": 5.98 },
      { "str": " ", "x": 113.98, "y": 710.04, "width": 11.96 },
      { "str": "Introduction", "x": 125.93, "y": 710.04, "width": 64.88 },
      { "str": "", "x": 108, "y": 685.35, "width": 0 },
      {
        "str": "Recurrent neural networks, long short-term memory [13] and gated recurrent [7] neural networks",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 685.35,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "in particular, have been firmly established as state of the art approaches in sequence modeling and",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 674.45,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "transduction problems such as language modeling and machine translation [35, 2, 5]. Numerous",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 663.54,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "efforts have since continued to push the boundaries of recurrent language models and encoder-decoder",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 652.63,
        "width": 396.17
      },
      {
        "str": "architectures [38, 24, 15].",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 641.72,
        "width": 102.37
      },
      {
        "str": "Recurrent models typically factor computation along the symbol positions of the input and output",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 625.33,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "sequences. Aligning the positions to steps in computation time, they generate a sequence of hidden",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 614.42,
        "width": 396
      },
      { "str": "states", "x": 108, "y": 603.51, "width": 21.92 },
      { "str": " ", "x": 129.92, "y": 603.51, "width": 2.49 },
      { "str": "h", "x": 132.41, "y": 603.51, "width": 5.74 },
      { "str": "t", "x": 138.15, "y": 602.02, "width": 3.01 },
      {
        "str": ", as a function of the previous hidden state",
        "x": 141.65,
        "y": 603.51,
        "width": 166.77
      },
      { "str": " ", "x": 308.43, "y": 603.51, "width": 2.49 },
      { "str": "h", "x": 310.92, "y": 603.51, "width": 5.74 },
      { "str": "t", "x": 316.66, "y": 602.02, "width": 3.01 },
      { "str": "−", "x": 319.67, "y": 602.02, "width": 6.23 },
      { "str": "1", "x": 325.9, "y": 602.02, "width": 3.97 },
      { "str": " ", "x": 329.87, "y": 602.02, "width": 3.02 },
      {
        "str": "and the input for position",
        "x": 332.86,
        "y": 603.51,
        "width": 99.82
      },
      { "str": " ", "x": 432.68, "y": 603.51, "width": 2.49 },
      { "str": "t", "x": 435.17, "y": 603.51, "width": 3.6 },
      { "str": ". This inherently", "x": 438.77, "y": 603.51, "width": 65.58 },
      {
        "str": "sequential nature precludes parallelization within training examples, which becomes critical at longer",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 592.6,
        "width": 396.17
      },
      {
        "str": "sequence lengths, as memory constraints limit batching across examples. Recent work has achieved",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 581.69,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "significant improvements in computational efficiency through factorization tricks [21] and conditional",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 570.78,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "computation [32], while also improving model performance in case of the latter. The fundamental",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 559.88,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "constraint of sequential computation, however, remains.",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 548.97,
        "width": 222.52
      },
      {
        "str": "Attention mechanisms have become an integral part of compelling sequence modeling and transduc-",
        "x": 107.64,
        "y": 532.58,
        "width": 398.01
      },
      {
        "str": "tion models in various tasks, allowing modeling of dependencies without regard to their distance in",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 521.67,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "the input or output sequences [2, 19]. In all but a few cases [27], however, such attention mechanisms",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 510.76,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "are used in conjunction with a recurrent network.",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 499.85,
        "width": 195.79
      },
      {
        "str": "In this work we propose the Transformer, a model architecture eschewing recurrence and instead",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 483.46,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "relying entirely on an attention mechanism to draw global dependencies between input and output.",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 472.55,
        "width": 397.74
      },
      {
        "str": "The Transformer allows for significantly more parallelization and can reach a new state of the art in",
        "x": 107.69,
        "y": 461.64,
        "width": 396.31
      },
      {
        "str": "translation quality after being trained for as little as twelve hours on eight P100 GPUs.",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 450.73,
        "width": 344.36
      },
      { "str": "", "x": 108, "y": 419.72, "width": 0 },
      { "str": "2", "x": 108, "y": 419.72, "width": 5.98 },
      { "str": " ", "x": 113.98, "y": 419.72, "width": 11.96 },
      { "str": "Background", "x": 125.93, "y": 419.72, "width": 62.9 },
      { "str": "", "x": 107.69, "y": 395.04, "width": 0 },
      {
        "str": "The goal of reducing sequential computation also forms the foundation of the Extended Neural GPU",
        "x": 107.69,
        "y": 395.04,
        "width": 396.31
      },
      {
        "str": "[16], ByteNet [18] and ConvS2S [9], all of which use convolutional neural networks as basic building",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 384.13,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "block, computing hidden representations in parallel for all input and output positions. In these models,",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 373.22,
        "width": 397.24
      },
      {
        "str": "the number of operations required to relate signals from two arbitrary input or output positions grows",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 362.31,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "in the distance between positions, linearly for ConvS2S and logarithmically for ByteNet. This makes",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 351.4,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "it more difficult to learn dependencies between distant positions [12]. In the Transformer this is",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 340.5,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "reduced to a constant number of operations, albeit at the cost of reduced effective resolution due",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 329.59,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "to averaging attention-weighted positions, an effect we counteract with Multi-Head Attention as",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 318.68,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "described in section 3.2.",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 307.77,
        "width": 96.57
      },
      {
        "str": "Self-attention, sometimes called intra-attention is an attention mechanism relating different positions",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 291.38,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "of a single sequence in order to compute a representation of the sequence. Self-attention has been",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 280.47,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "used successfully in a variety of tasks including reading comprehension, abstractive summarization,",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 269.56,
        "width": 397.25
      },
      {
        "str": "textual entailment and learning task-independent sentence representations [4, 27, 28, 22].",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 258.65,
        "width": 355.12
      },
      {
        "str": "End-to-end memory networks are based on a recurrent attention mechanism instead of sequence-",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 242.26,
        "width": 397.65
      },
      {
        "str": "aligned recurrence and have been shown to perform well on simple-language question answering and",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 231.36,
        "width": 395.99
      },
      {
        "str": "language modeling tasks [34].",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 220.45,
        "width": 120.09
      },
      {
        "str": "To the best of our knowledge, however, the Transformer is the first transduction model relying",
        "x": 107.69,
        "y": 204.06,
        "width": 396.31
      },
      {
        "str": "entirely on self-attention to compute representations of its input and output without using sequence-",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 193.15,
        "width": 397.66
      },
      {
        "str": "aligned RNNs or convolution. In the following sections, we will describe the Transformer, motivate",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 182.24,
        "width": 396
      },
      {
        "str": "self-attention and discuss its advantages over models such as [17, 18] and [9].",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 171.33,
        "width": 309.35
      },
      { "str": "", "x": 108, "y": 140.32, "width": 0 },
      { "str": "3", "x": 108, "y": 140.32, "width": 5.98 },
      { "str": " ", "x": 113.98, "y": 140.32, "width": 11.96 },
      {
        "str": "Model Architecture",
        "x": 125.93,
        "y": 140.32,
        "width": 100.16
      },
      { "str": "", "x": 108, "y": 115.64, "width": 0 },
      {
        "str": "Most competitive neural sequence transduction models have an encoder-decoder structure [5, 2, 35].",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 115.64,
        "width": 397.74
      },
      {
        "str": "Here, the encoder maps an input sequence of symbol representations",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 104.73,
        "width": 286.63
      },
      { "str": " ", "x": 394.63, "y": 104.73, "width": 3.38 },
      { "str": "(", "x": 398.01, "y": 104.73, "width": 3.87 },
      { "str": "x", "x": 401.88, "y": 104.73, "width": 5.69 },
      { "str": "1", "x": 407.57, "y": 103.23, "width": 3.97 },
      { "str": ", ..., x", "x": 412.04, "y": 104.73, "width": 22.85 },
      { "str": "n", "x": 434.89, "y": 103.23, "width": 4.92 },
      { "str": ")", "x": 440.32, "y": 104.73, "width": 3.87 },
      { "str": " ", "x": 444.19, "y": 104.73, "width": 3.32 },
      { "str": "to a sequence", "x": 447.57, "y": 104.73, "width": 56.43 },
      {
        "str": "of continuous representations",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 93.82,
        "width": 121.96
      },
      { "str": " ", "x": 229.96, "y": 93.82, "width": 3.7 },
      { "str": "z", "x": 233.66, "y": 93.82, "width": 5.09 },
      { "str": " ", "x": 238.75, "y": 93.82, "width": 4.99 },
      { "str": "= (", "x": 243.74, "y": 93.82, "width": 16.61 },
      { "str": "z", "x": 260.35, "y": 93.82, "width": 4.63 },
      { "str": "1", "x": 264.99, "y": 92.32, "width": 3.97 },
      { "str": ", ..., z", "x": 269.46, "y": 93.82, "width": 21.79 },
      { "str": "n", "x": 291.25, "y": 92.32, "width": 4.92 },
      { "str": ")", "x": 296.67, "y": 93.82, "width": 3.87 },
      { "str": ".", "x": 300.55, "y": 93.82, "width": 2.54 },
      { "str": " ", "x": 303.09, "y": 93.82, "width": 6.56 },
      { "str": "Given", "x": 309.77, "y": 93.82, "width": 24.44 },
      { "str": " ", "x": 334.21, "y": 93.82, "width": 3.69 },
      { "str": "z", "x": 337.9, "y": 93.82, "width": 5.09 },
      {
        "str": ", the decoder then generates an output",
        "x": 343,
        "y": 93.82,
        "width": 161
      },
      { "str": "sequence", "x": 108, "y": 82.91, "width": 37.24 },
      { "str": " ", "x": 145.24, "y": 82.91, "width": 2.56 },
      { "str": "(", "x": 147.8, "y": 82.91, "width": 3.87 },
      { "str": "y", "x": 151.68, "y": 82.91, "width": 4.88 },
      { "str": "1", "x": 156.56, "y": 81.42, "width": 3.97 },
      { "str": ", ..., y", "x": 161.03, "y": 82.91, "width": 22.04 },
      { "str": "m", "x": 183.07, "y": 81.42, "width": 7.07 },
      { "str": ")", "x": 190.64, "y": 82.91, "width": 3.87 },
      { "str": " ", "x": 194.51, "y": 82.91, "width": 2.51 },
      {
        "str": "of symbols one element at a time. At each step the model is auto-regressive",
        "x": 197.07,
        "y": 82.91,
        "width": 306.93
      },
      {
        "str": "[10], consuming the previously generated symbols as additional input when generating the next.",
        "x": 108,
        "y": 72,
        "width": 382.56
      },
      { "str": "2", "x": 303.51, "y": 42.11, "width": 4.98 }
    ]
